  "body": "The maintainer reported the defects in chat on 2026-11-15, on v0.21.0 (first filed as #1994). His words:\n\n> turn the icons back to white.. Nobody can see blue on gray\n\n> change them to white as well.. and the text \"Milling 2d, MILLING 3D, etc etc\" need som space..\n\nHe then decided that the correction belongs in the themes, not in the general UI code:\n\n> That issue.. 1994 and its PR 1999 - should then be abandoned.. and the correction should happen in the two new themes rather.\n\n## What happens\n\nSince commit `37e7594ec` (\"a light workbench theme and workspace tabs\", 2026-11-14) the ribbon icons are blue on a grey background and are hard to see. The workspace tab row and the group captions (\"Milling 2D\", \"Milling 3D\") have too little space.\n\n## What to do\n\nCorrect this in the theme data, not in the shell code:\n\n- The theme files are `assets/themes/horizon-day.json` and `assets/themes/teal-night.json`, with the built-in tables in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/theme.rs`. Confirm with the maintainer's words above which two themes he means, if more exist when you start.\n- Each theme gives the icon ink for the ribbon cells, the tree and the toolbars. A dark theme uses white icons. A light theme uses an ink that reads on its background.\n- Each theme gives the height of the ribbon rows, so that the workspace tabs and the captions have space.\n- The shell code reads these values from the theme. It contains no colour literal and no row height of its own (see #1120).\n\nPR #1999 was closed without a merge. Its diff (branch `issue/1994-ribbon-rows-white-icons`) shows where the shell reads the ink and the row heights. Do not copy its hard-coded values.\n\n## Done means\n\n- In each of the two themes, the ribbon icons read clearly on the ribbon background.\n- The workspace tabs and the group captions have space in each theme, at 1280x720.\n- A structural test pins, for each theme, the icon ink against the background (a contrast minimum) and that the tab row and the captions do not overlap.\n- The PR body has before and after images for each theme, rendered offscreen.\n",
